  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x+y)=f(x) \\cdot f(y) \\forall x \\cdot y$ and $f(5)=2, f^{\\prime}(0)=3$ then $f^{\\prime}(5)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rcMMg",
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JcO9a",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5y8wx",
      "text": "\n6\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "E98co",
      "text": "\n2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nf(x+y)=f(x) \\times f(y)\n$$\nDifferentiate with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as constant\n$$\nf^{\\prime}(x+y)=f(x) f(y)\n$$\nPutting $x=0$ and $y=x$, we get $f^{\\prime}(x)=f^{\\prime}(0) f(x) ; \\Rightarrow f^{\\prime}(5)=3 f(5)=3 \\times 2=6$",
    "image": null
  },
